Hermione's reunification there were  suddenly 16 million more people living  in the federal republic the change was a  huge financial challenge to the health  care and Social Security system the new  citizens were insured from the beginning  also receiving pensions and unemployment  compensation the ailing economy in East  Germany left its mark many factories  were ready for closure and 70% of all  rivers were contaminated the creation of  the unity fund totaling some 80 billion  euros was aimed at financing the new  challenges the first solidarity pact  added another 95 billion euros to clean  up mining areas dismantle nuclear power  plants and renovate buildings it also  funded new roads and railway lines some  work has yet to be done  the second solidarity pact takes effect  in 2019 the government plans to pump  nearly 160 billion euros into the East's  infrastructure experts estimate that  since reunification some two trillion  euros from Berlin and Brussels have been  spent on propping up eastern Germany
 

